	(text "Notes\n1. Modulino Light on the UNO Q's Qwiic connector: bus Wire1, address 0x53. A Modulino Movement may stay\n    on the chain (address 0x6A); the test ignores it.\n2. D1 faces the Modulino Light's sensor window 1-3 cm away. Both sit inside a short black tube or box\n    (light-tight). A sheet of paper in between spreads the light and keeps it from saturating the sensor.\n3. The sketch flashes D1 at known rates (1-35 Hz square waves, 5 ms and 1 ms flashes) and reads the sensor\n    at its maximum rate (nominally 40 readings/s; about 36 measured). It picks the sensor gain by itself.\n4. D1: white LED, current about (5 - 3.0 - 0.1 V) / 220 R = 9 mA. R2 limits the base current from the 3.3 V pin to about 2.6 mA.\n    Q1: any small NPN (2N3904, BC547, 2N2222); check the pinout, BC547 is C-B-E.\n5. Measured (screen sweep): correct frequency 1-15 Hz, 10 Hz exact; about 18 Hz is the limit;\n    20 / 25 / 30 Hz show up as about 16 / 11 / 6 Hz (DI-01).\n6. Safety: D1 flashes at seizure-provoking rates. Keep it inside the tube (DI-12)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 127 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
